{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/75846-defining-pillar-purchase-clarification","id":75846,"title":"Defining Pillar purchase clarification","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T13:32:42-08:00","id":75846,"title":"Defining Pillar purchase clarification","content":"On the Pilar Rules in Character Creation;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3E454C\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">No Pillar can be higher than the decree\u2019s defining Pillar, and only it may be raised to five dots during character creation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Does that mean that, as it reads, a mummy that starts with 3 dots in the defining pillar in character creation will NEVER be able to go past that pillar rating?<br /> There's even a special cost for raising a defining pillar, so this doesn't make sense to me. Why would they make it that way? Is there an errata or something that corrects that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2339-aethereas","name":"Aethereas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2339_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T13:44:33-08:00","id":75858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aethereas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/75846-defining-pillar-purchase-clarification#post75846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Pilar Rules in Character Creation;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3E454C\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">No Pillar can be higher than the decree\u2019s defining Pillar, and only it may be raised to five dots during character creation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Does that mean that, as it reads, a mummy that starts with 3 dots in the defining pillar in character creation will NEVER be able to go past that pillar rating?<br /> There's even a special cost for raising a defining pillar, so this doesn't make sense to me. Why would they make it that way? Is there an errata or something that corrects that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The defining Pillar is the only one you can start with at five dots. The rest of them can only be bought up as high as four dots, which is important primarily when considering that you can trade starting Merit dots for Pillars. After character creation you can increase any of your Pillar ratings with experience as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T14:10:57-08:00","id":75879,"title":"","content":"The book says, and you quote &quot;and only it may be raised&quot;<br /> <br /> If it meant that you could miss out on the chance for a 5, it'd say &quot;and it may only be raised&quot;<br /> <br /> (Yes, you can buy as many Pillars as you like with XP. You're only limited to the defining pillar at 5 and the rest at 4 in chargen)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T14:21:31-08:00","id":75887,"title":"","content":"Thanks, i see it was a reading mistake in my part, but in the &quot;Starting Pillars&quot; section, it also says;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3E454C\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Spending experience allows a player to have her character attain five dots in Pillars other than the decree\u2019s defining Pillar, but the mummy must still possess a dot or more in the other four.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Does this means that you cant invest XP in raising the defining pillar during character creation (due to it being written under &quot;Starting Pillars&quot; section) or is it, again, saying that you can't raise the defining pillar with XP to 5 after character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2339-aethereas","name":"Aethereas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2339_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T15:54:46-08:00","id":75930,"title":"","content":"No, it's saying that you <i>can</i> spend XP to raise any pillar. If you want two Pillars at five, you have to spend experience. In order to get <i>any</i> Pillar to 5, you can't have an empty Pillar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T13:22:12-07:00","id":97014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/75846-defining-pillar-purchase-clarification?p=75930#post75930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's saying that you <i>can</i> spend XP to raise any pillar. If you want two Pillars at five, you have to spend experience. In order to get <i>any</i> Pillar to 5, you can't have an empty Pillar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Not to sound like a dick, but I really don't get what the OP's questions are really about -- the text, as written, is pretty straight forward. (Unless English isn't the OP's primary language, in which case then some translational/usage error may be the issue -- *that* I totally understand...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}